# /root/harness/env/github-app.env — GitHub App installation tokens. chmod 600.
# NEVER in git (env/ is gitignored for exactly this reason).
#
# WHAT THIS BUYS (the operator, 2026-09-14). Without this file every lane on every box
# and every ephemeral Fly builder authenticates GitHub with ONE personal access
# token, so the whole fleet shares one 5000-request/hour bucket and one
# credential that never expires. With it, bin/gh-token.sh mints a token scoped to
# a single repo that dies in an hour, rate-limited per INSTALLATION instead of
# per account. Setup is one-time and operator-only: docs/OPERATOR-SETUP.md,
# "GitHub App installation tokens".
#
# The file's PRESENCE is the arm. Delete it, set GH_APP_TOKENS=0, or
# `touch flags/gh-app-tokens-off` and every lane falls back to the PAT it uses
# today — same calls, same behaviour, no deploy needed either way.

# The App's numeric id, from its settings page ("App ID", not the client id).
GH_APP_ID=<numeric-app-id>

# The .pem you downloaded when you generated the App's private key. chmod 600.
GH_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/root/harness/env/github-app.pem

# Kill switch that needs no file deletion. 1 (or unset) = mint App tokens.
GH_APP_TOKENS=1

# OPTIONAL, and only if you did NOT name the App `cromford`. A PR opened on
# an installation token is authored by the App, and every consumer that finds
# harness PRs recognises them by the author set HARNESS_PR_AUTHORS (default
# "operator app/cromford", bin/lib/gh-pr-list.sh). Naming the slug here unions
# `app/<slug>` into that set, so nothing else has to be configured.
# GH_APP_SLUG=cromford

# OPTIONAL, one per owner the App is installed on: the installation id, so the
# box never has to spend a GET /app/installations to find it. The variable name
# is the owner upper-cased with - and . turned into _:
#   GH_APP_INSTALLATION_example-org=<installation-id>
#   GH_APP_INSTALLATION_project-7=<installation-id>
# Read them off:  gh api /app/installations  (or the App's install page URL).
# Left unset, bin/gh-token.sh discovers them once and caches the answer in
# state/gh-app-installations.json.
